#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# permutation_group

#% text
# `permutation_group([g1, ...])`: the group generated by the permutations; permutation_group(F), (F, H): a finitely presented group acting on the cosets of H

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A permutation group is given by generators; it acts on 1, ..., n with n the largest moved point.

#% item
# `permutation_group(F)` is the action of a finitely presented group on the cosets of the trivial subgroup (its regular representation); `permutation_group(F, H)` the action on the cosets of the subgroup generated by the words H.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
g = permutation_group([cycles([[1, 2, 3, 4]]), cycles([[1, 3]])])

#% cell
group_order(g)
#% output
#= 8

#% cell
group_degree(permutation_group(finitely_presented_group([a, b], [a^2, b^3, table([a, b], 5)])))
#% output
#= 60

#% cell
group_order(permutation_group(finitely_presented_group([a, b], [a^2, b^3, table([a, b], 5)]), [b]))
#% output
#= 60

